{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.fandm.edu/faculty-center/index.html": {
      "title": "Faculty Center",
      "description": "Faculty Center Franklin & Marshall Faculty Center Home / Faculty Center Supporting, Sustaining, and Celebrating Faculty At F&M, we support, sustain and celebrate faculty in their roles as teachers, scholars,\n                        and college citizens. Our Faculty Center focuses on faculty development and is specifically\n                        dedicated to offering pedagogical and scholarly support as well as building community\n                        through informal interaction. We strive to be the first line of support for our F&M faculty through our programming\n                        and resources, including: New faculty orientation during which offices across campus provide group and individual\n                           support for our new faculty colleagues on topics relating to pedagogy, scholarship\n                           and being a part of the F&M community, as well as the general higher education field. Monthly workshops and events covering topics such as pedagogy, grant seeking, time\n                           management, advising, leadership, and more Writing circles, reading groups, and other collaborative faculty working groups Private consultations offering a confidential, non-evaluative setting to discuss common\n                           faculty issues, including mid-semester course reviews, syllabus design, work-life\n                           balance, department chair concerns and maintaining scholarship A small library of volumes specifically selected on pedagogy and faculty life Grants and Funding The Faculty Center offers financial support to F&M faculty members for innovative\n                                 work at the class, course, and curricular levels. We also support collaborative projects\n                                 important to faculty on our campus. Recent examples include addressing mid-career\n                                 faculty issues, equity in STEM disciplines, social justice, and power dynamics in\n                                 the curriculum. Those embarking on larger projects can turn to F&M’s Office of Sponsored Research for support navigating and facilitating sponsored funding opportunities from internal\n                                 sources as well as federal, state, and nonprofit organizations. Learn more about grants and funding Turning a Dream into Reality The Faculty Center is the culmination of a faculty-driven initiative. The project\n                                    began in 2013 to enhance our extraordinary teaching and learning tradition and fuel\n                                    knowledge, discovery, and artistic creation. The Andrew W. Mellon Foundation awarded\n                                    a $700,000 grant to provide startup operating support to the Faculty Center. Today, we continue this mission and work hand-in-hand with our many campus partners\n                                    to offer a wide array of programs to address the varied professional development needs\n                                    of our faculty. The Arthur Vining Davis Foundations awarded the Faculty Center a grant\n                                    to help us rise to the challenge of identifying tools and strategies to prepare today's\n                                    students for success in an increasingly global, knowledge-based society. Academics Explore Programs Admission & Aid Learn More Our campus Plan Your Visit Our website has been designed with accessibility in mind and incorporates many accessible\n                     features. If you are experiencing difficulty accessing a College website, or content\n                     located on a College website (video, document, etc.), please contact us at websters@fandm.edu.\n                     The College does not make representations with regard to the accessibility of third-party\n                     websites and is not able to remediate accessibility barriers on such websites. © 2026 Franklin & Marshall College P.O. Box 3003, Lancaster, PA 17604-3003 General Information: 717-358-3911 facebook twitter instagram linkedin PRIVACY POLICY | Calendar Give Careers F&M Bookstore Contact F&M News and Stories Nondiscrimination Community & Belonging Privacy Events Fields of Study F&M Experience Portal JavaScript is required to view this site. Please enable JavaScript to continue browsing. ©"
    },
    "https://www.fandm.edu/career-and-professional-development/index.html": {
      "title": "Center for Career and Professional Development",
      "description": "Center for Career and Professional Development Franklin & Marshall Center for Career and Professional Development Home / Center for Career and Professional Development The Center for Career and Professional Development cultivates professional development\n                           experiences that embolden students and alumni to design and navigate fulfilling careers\n                           with courage and curiosity. Navigation Career Communities Programs & Services Experience Lancaster Success Beyond F&M Contact Discover Your Calling. Grow in Community. F&M's liberal arts model is at the heart of our Center for Career and Professional Development: receiving\n                           targeted, expert guidance while exploring a wide range of post-graduate paths to discover\n                           your professional calling and develop the skills you need to succeed. To help you\n                           navigate this exploration and discovery, our career guidance is structured through\n                           “career communities” – dynamic groups aligned with specific industries that transform\n                           your aspirations into clear options, meaningful opportunities, and a network of support. You can join a career community that speaks to your calling, and even move freely\n                        between communities as your interests and plans naturally evolve. This model helps\n                        you to begin your career discernment process right away, and allow it to run parallel\n                        to and intersect with your entire undergraduate experience. You'll always have a place\n                        to belong as you find your way, gaining professional and expert insights, connections\n                        to experiential learning opportunities, direct access to an engaged network of successful\n                        alumni in the field, and a supportive community of fellow Diplomats who share your\n                        interests and professional goals. Career Communities Business & Finance Are you ready to lead with vision, drive success, and bring transformative ideas to\n                                             life? The Career Center provides expert support and guidance to help you succeed in business and finance. Gain insight through our workshops and programs, build hands-on experience\n                                             and enhance your resume with internships , and be part of a strong community of peers who share your drive. Law & Government Professions Are you passionate about making a difference through public service? Careers in law, government , consulting and public policy are crucial for protecting rights, upholding justice, serving constituents, innovating\n                                             solutions, and shaping the future of our society. The Career Center offers outstanding\n                                             resources — including workshops, internship support, and a pre-law program — to help you cultivate the skills and experiences you need to prosper in these fields. Health Professions Healthcare offers diverse pathways to make a difference through science, compassion,\n                                             and innovation. If you’re considering a career in this vital field, you’ll find unrivaled\n                                             support from the Career Center, including in-depth workshops, clinical and shadowing\n                                             opportunities, medical school admission test preparation, early assurance programs,\n                                             and more. Pre-Dental Do you want to make a difference in people’s lives by improving their oral hygiene\n                                             and health? Be a part of F&M’s pre-dental program and set yourself up for a successful\n                                             career in dentistry. Explore Pre-Dental at F&M Pre-Health Whether you’re considering a career as a physician assistant, physical therapist,\n                                             pharmacist, optometrist, or other vital role in the field of medicine, you’ll find\n                                             the support you need in F&M’s pre-health program. Explore Pre-Health at F&M Pre-Medical Begin your career in an essential, effective, and rewarding field. By participating\n                                             in F&M’s pre-medical program, you’ll find all the guidance and support you need to\n                                             build a sturdy foundation for a successful future in medicine. Explore Pre-Med at F&M Pre-Veterinary F&M’s pre-veterinary program has a legacy of preparing students for successful careers\n                                             in veterinary medicine, empowering you to provide compassionate care to your animal\n                                             patients while cultivating strong relationships with the animals’ owners. Explore Pre-Vet at F&M Social Impact & Creative Careers Shape minds, contribute to a vibrant society, and build a better future. Careers in\n                                             the arts, education, and emerging field of social impact are vital for empowering\n                                             learners, launching innovative solutions, fostering understanding, and strengthening\n                                             communities. If you're drawn to making change through creativity, the Career Center\n                                             offers tailored resources — including workshops and connections to real-world experiences\n                                             — to help you thrive in these meaningful fields. STEM Innovate, build, and explore. Careers in science, technology, engineering, and math\n                                             (STEM) are fast-growing and ever-changing, offering exciting opportunities to advance\n                                             technology, solve complex global challenges, design groundbreaking solutions, and\n                                             shape the future of our world. If you’re driven to create the future through ingenuity,\n                                             you’ll find expert support from the Career Center, including comprehensive workshops,\n                                             access to hands-on research and internships, our engineering dual degree program , and networking with alumni who are leaders in their fields. What Can I Do With This Major? An F&M liberal arts education prepares you to be world-ready, equipping you with transferrable\n                                       skills to excel in not just one career, but many. This model is specifically built\n                                       for exploration, empowering you to design an academic path precisely tailored to your\n                                       interests and goals. Dive into what awaits you with What Can I Do With This Major? , a tool that helps connect your interests to future possibilities with 100 profiles\n                                       on career paths, employers, and opportunity-maximizing strategies. Read More » Success Beyond F&M Within six months after graduation, 92% of the Class of 2025 were either employed\n                                 or furthering their education. This is higher than the national average, which is\n                                 typically in the mid-80% range. You can rest assured that at F&M, you’ll find your footing on campus and beyond. Our\n                                 enduring commitment to your success helps you land jobs in leading industries and\n                                 gain admission to high-demand graduate and professional programs around the world. Explore Outcomes Experience Lancaster To shape the world, start right where you are. Our home city of Lancaster is not only an active urban center, but also an integral educational partner. Experience\n                                 Lancaster, a program distinct to F&M, curates and connects you with opportunities\n                                 to engage in internships, service, research, and more so you can make an impact in\n                                 your own backyard. Experience Lancaster Programs and Services In addition to our career communities, we also offer programs and activities that\n                        are purposefully designed to launch you to success. They include leadership development,\n                        financial literacy, major exploration, internship support, and post-graduate success\n                        planning. Student Advising Each career community has a dedicated adviser with expertise in the field. Your adviser\n                                       will help you explore your career options by talking through your strengths, interests,\n                                       and goals; work with you to develop a customized goal-oriented plan; help you discover\n                                       and land professional development experiences; perfect your application materials;\n                                       and more. Programming & Events The Career Center offers innovative and engaging programs on life skills such as personal\n                                       finance, public speaking, leadership development and more, and hosts a variety of\n                                       career-related events to introduce you to a breadth of post-graduate options. Our\n                                       most popular events include: “Not a Major Decision” workshops and academic fair designed to help sophomores in\n                                             their major declaration Leadership seminars “Living Beyond F&M Series” consisting of sessions on financial literacy, public speaking,\n                                             the etiquette of the business meal, and more Night of Networking Job & Internship Fair Senior Boot Camp Alumni Advising Your time at F&M was a transformational experience that helped to forge the path you\n                                       are on today — a path that can often pivot in ways you don’t expect. No matter your\n                                       goals — whether you’re securing your first job, applying to graduate school, or contemplating\n                                       a career change — alumni advisers are available for you. Explore alumni advising » Internship Support Gain experience now and a competitive advantage later. Internships allow you to explore\n                                       fields and job functions of interest, building your portfolio while shaping and inspiring\n                                       your path. The Career Center will help you discover and land these positions, guiding\n                                       you through the internship search, application, and interview processes, and facilitating\n                                       connections with F&M alumni, parents and friends of the College for potential opportunities. LEARN MORE “Before consulting the Career Center’s student services, I felt overwhelmed about\n                                                all that I needed to do to secure a summer internship. Working with the Career Center\n                                                staff made the search for internships more approachable and eased my fears about the\n                                                application process. ” — Julia Kait ’23 F&M Works F&M Works in Lancaster is a selective program designed for you to explore your understanding\n                                       of personal and social responsibility. You’ll contribute to the community by working\n                                       as an intern at a local nonprofit organization, and engage in meaningful discussions\n                                       with a cohort of like-minded students about values, belonging, community and leadership\n                                       — all within the context of exploring the common good. Students participating in F&M\n                                       Works in Lancaster are paid by the College. Service Opportunities Explore what it means to be a thoughtful and active member of a community. F&M’s Ware\n                                       Institute for Civic Engagement connects F&M students with opportunities to serve dozens\n                                       of nonprofits and agencies in the surrounding Lancaster community. LEARN MORE » The Franklin Fellowship The Franklin Fellowship is an exclusive opportunity at the University of Pennsylvania’s\n                                       Graduate School of Education (GSE) reserved for recent graduates of Franklin & Marshall\n                                       College interested in long-term teaching in Philadelphia. Students applying for the Urban Teaching Residency M.S.Ed. program at Penn are eligible\n                                       to apply for the fellowship, which includes a $15,000 scholarship that can be combined\n                                       other merit or need-based scholarships at Penn’s GSE. LEARN MORE » Student Employment Each year, more than 1,000 students seek on-campus employment in a wide variety of\n                                       positions. These positions are more than just jobs; they are opportunities to build\n                                       relationships and communication skills while developing your toolkit for careers after\n                                       F&M. If you’re enrolled in at least three credits per semester (a full-time course load),\n                                       you are eligible for on-campus employment. If you are awarded Federal Work Study or\n                                       College Work Option in your financial aid package, you are given priority status as\n                                       an aided student and are eligible to apply for any position on campus. If you’re not\n                                       work-aided, you are still eligible to work on campus, but will have a limited number\n                                       of positions available to you. F&M’s Student Employment Office (SEO) will guide you\n                                       through the position search and hiring process, and match you with positions where\n                                       you will learn valuable, transferable skills that will benefit you both at F&M and\n                                       beyond. If you have questions about student employment at F&M, you can reach out to studentemployment@fandm.edu . “The opportunities provided to me at F&M, both inside and outside of the classroom,\n                                    have crafted me into the young professional that I am.” — Munahil Sultana ’24, Former President of Diplomatic Congress, Pickering Fellow,\n                                    and Voyager Scholar F&M Launches Students Toward Success September 8, 2026 Lancaster Internship Shapes Pre-Law Path Molly DeBrandt ’28 transformed academic curiosity into career conviction. As an intern with the Office of the Public Defender of Lancaster County, she stepped directly into the daily realities of public defense and discovered a passion for law. “I now intend to apply to law school following my graduation from F&M,” she said. Read More » August 31, 2026 Fulfilling a Dream: A Diplomat’s Forensic Internship For Kayla McCrea ’27, the path to forensic science began with a high school tour of the New Jersey State Police. Emboldened by that early glimpse into the field, she came to F&M to build the expertise and skills necessary to return as a toxicology unit intern — a feat she accomplished this summer. Read More » August 24, 2026 F&M and Fulton Bank: Where Liberal Arts and Innovation Meet For Moemen Ibrahim ’26, an assignment to reach out to a Franklin & Marshall College alumna on LinkedIn led to much more than a career conversation. It became the beginning of an internship and an introduction to the world of innovation at Fulton Bank — and has also led to a full-time job. Read More » Contact the Career Center Meet Our Team Lucy Deren Assistant Director, Ware Institute for Civic Engagement Contact » Keri Fritsch Program Coordinator, Center for Career & Professional Development Contact » Ashley C Fry Director of Business/Finance Professions Advising & Data Assessment Contact » Sarah Gall Director of Pre-Health Professions Advising Contact » Beth Grimm Director of STEM Professions Advising Contact » Angela Harnish Director of Social Impact & Creative Professions Advising Contact » Kathryn M Hertzler Assistant Manager of Student Employment Contact » Keo Oura Kounlavong-Sabath Director of Student Employment Contact » Stephanie M McConnell Executive Director of Career & Professional Development Contact » Mike Vitlip Director of Legal & Government Professions Advising Contact » Hire a Diplomat Intern If you’re looking to connect with students or recent graduates who have exceptional\n                                          writing, analytical, critical thinking, and creative skills, you’ve come to the right\n                                          place. Fill out this form to learn how you can post an opportunity or recruit on campus. LEARN MORE » True Blue Network True Blue Network for Students When you enroll at F&M, you become part of the F&Mily: a network of tens of thousands\n                                          of alumni, families and friends of the College. The True Blue Network — a career network\n                                          platform exclusive to our community — is a powerful resource connecting thousands\n                                          members of the F&Mily who consistently raise their hands to recruit, mentor, refer\n                                          and guide Diplomats during and beyond their time at F&M. Here, you can connect with\n                                          alumni and parents who have volunteered to support student success beyond the classroom,\n                                          including internship and career opportunities. True Blue Network for Alumni, Parents & Friends Whether you’re sharing an internship, a part-time job, a fellowship, or an opportunity\n                                          for a full-time career, you can use True Blue Network to help launch an F&M student\n                                          or recent graduate toward success. Academics Explore Programs Admission & Aid Learn More Our campus Plan Your Visit Our website has been designed with accessibility in mind and incorporates many accessible\n                     features. If you are experiencing difficulty accessing a College website, or content\n                     located on a College website (video, document, etc.), please contact us at websters@fandm.edu.\n                     The College does not make representations with regard to the accessibility of third-party\n                     websites and is not able to remediate accessibility barriers on such websites. © 2026 Franklin & Marshall College P.O. Box 3003, Lancaster, PA 17604-3003 General Information: 717-358-3911 facebook twitter instagram linkedin PRIVACY POLICY | Calendar Give Careers F&M Bookstore Contact F&M News and Stories Nondiscrimination Community & Belonging Privacy Events Fields of Study F&M Experience Portal JavaScript is required to view this site. Please enable JavaScript to continue browsing. ©"
    },
